      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "The edge length of a square can be expressed in two different ways, so we can set these two expressions equal to each other and solve for $x$:\n\\[4x-15=20-3x\\]\nAdding $3x$ to both sides and adding 15 to both sides, we get:\n\\[7x=35\\]\nDividing both sides by 7, we find:\n\\[x=5\\]\nSubstituting $x=5$ into either expression for the edge length, we find:\n\\[4x-15=4(5)-15=10-15=-5\\]\nSince the edge length cannot be negative, we take the absolute value:\n\\[|-5|=5\\]\nThe area of the square is the square of the edge length, so the area is:\n\\[5^2=\\boxed{25}\\] square meters.\nThe answer is: 25",
