      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "1. The sum of the lengths of the two adjacent sides of a square is 40 meters. Therefore, we can set up the equation:\n\\[ (4x-15) + (20-3x) = 40 \\]\n\n2. Simplify the equation:\n\\[ 4x - 3x + 20 - 15 = 40 \\]\n\\[ x + 5 = 40 \\]\n\n3. Solve for $x$:\n\\[ x = 40 - 5 \\]\n\\[ x = 35 \\]\n\n4. Now that we have the value of $x$, we can find the length of one side of the square:\n\\[ 4x - 15 = 4(35) - 15 = 140 - 15 = 125 \\]\n\n5. The area of the square is the side length squared:\n\\[ 125 \\times 125 = 15625 \\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the square is $\\boxed{15625}$ square meters.",
